<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
     Arriving platform, moving FORWARD (the right chevron).

     A full-width slide in from the right, no fade. The board is one surface
     sliding sideways, the way every pager on the phone behaves, so the motion
     says "the next platform" rather than "something changed".

     ## How a directional slide is possible at all
     `setInAnimation` is not a @RemotableViewMethod, so a ViewFlipper's
     animation pair is fixed when the layout is inflated and cannot be chosen
     per tap. This file used to be a fade-and-rise for exactly that reason: one
     flipper can only have one animation, and a slide that travelled the same
     way whichever arrow you pressed was worse than not sliding.

     The answer is not one flipper but three, one per motion, stacked in the
     same slot with one visible — see widget_departure_board.xml. Each carries
     its own pair here, and the update picks a motion by picking a flipper.

     200ms: long enough to read as travel, short enough that pressing the arrow
     twice does not queue up a wait.
-->
<translate xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:duration="200"
    android:fromXDelta="100%p"
    android:interpolator="@android:interpolator/decelerate_quad"
    android:toXDelta="0" />
